  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "France 24 reports that Tripoli is demanding an explanation from Kyiv for striking Russian ships in Libyan waters.",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:e55baa58ddf4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:09Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera has also covered the story, asking where Ukraine might strike Russia next.",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:410f24ca4d1e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:18Z",
      "text": "Inflation in Ukraine was 12.7% in 2025, down from 20.2% in 2022.",
      "cites": [
        "wb:FP.CPI.TOTL.ZG:UA"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:26Z",
      "text": "The economy grew 1.8% in 2025, and unemployment stood at 9.8%.",
      "cites": [
        "wb:NY.GDP.MKTP.KD.ZG:UA",
        "wb:SL.UEM.TOTL.ZS:UA"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:36Z",
      "text": "Across Europe and Central Asia, Ukraine's 12.7% compares with a median of 3.8%, while the highest is Turkey at 34.9%.",
      "cites": [
        "wb:FP.CPI.TOTL.ZG:region:europe-central-asia"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:50Z",
      "text": "On 18 November, Ukrainian forces struck the Crimean Bridge for the third time in four days, and Russian authorities closed it to all traffic.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-18:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:57Z",
      "text": "On 22 November, several people were killed and at least 10 were injured when the Russian corvette Merkury was struck by a Ukrainian naval drone attack while docked at Benghazi, Libya.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-22:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:01:04Z",
      "text": "On 23 November, Ukraine launched a large-scale drone attack across western Russia, striking the Perm refinery and the Novoshakhtinsk refinery.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-23:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:01:12Z",
      "text": "Ukraine is the second-largest country in Europe after Russia, which borders it to the east and northeast.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386666930:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:01:23Z",
      "text": "France 24 headlined its report: “Live: Tripoli demands explanation from Kyiv for striking Russian ships in Libyan waters”.",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:e55baa58ddf4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:01:30Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera headlined its piece: “After Libya, where will Ukraine strike Russia next?”",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:410f24ca4d1e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:01:39Z",
      "text": "This explainer draws on 2 outlets, Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageviews, and Wikidata, with Wikipedia Portal:Current events pages for 2026 November 18 and 2026 November 22.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386666930:0",
        "views:en:Ukraine:30d",
        "wd:Q212:P571",
        "wiki:2026-11-18:1",
        "wiki:2026-11-22:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:01:40Z",
      "text": "Every caption links to the evidence it rests on.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386666930:0"
      ]
    }
  ],
